Spec: Terminal

Purpose:
  Let a person turn candidate scenes and photos into one saved post.

Owns:
  ./main.rs
  ./tui.rs

Must:
  Load settings, then apply flag and environment overrides in memory.
  A named path that is missing fails and names the field.
  Two empty media folders fail.
  List candidate segments and photos.
  The person trims a segment, groups cards, sets the kind, and edits the caption.
  Save writes plan.json under the out folder and calls render for that post.
  One key creates or deletes the empty chosen file on a saved post.
  One key opens that post in the system viewer. On macOS the command is open.
  The settings screen edits advise, api_base, model, api_key, and the three folders, then writes the settings file.
  The key field is masked.
  iPhone .heic and .mov files are accepted. A cloud-only placeholder fails and names the path.

Must not:
  Play video in the terminal.
  Mark a post chosen while listing candidates.
  Encode a candidate that the person has not saved.
  Call the network itself.

Depends on:
  ./settings.sdd
  ./inventory.sdd
  ./segments.sdd
  ./render.sdd
  ./advise.sdd

Scenario: save one post
  Given three candidate segments from one clip
  When the person groups two of them into a Story and saves
  Then the out folder contains that Story
  And the third segment is not encoded

Scenario: chosen toggle
  Given a saved post with no chosen file
  When the person toggles it
  Then an empty chosen file is in that post folder
  When the person toggles it again
  Then the chosen file is gone
